# Dress Down's ruling: "If an effect causes Dress Down to become a creature, it will lose its own abilities along with all
# other creatures. This includes the triggered ability that causes it to be sacrificed at the beginning of the end step."
# With Opalescence out, Dress Down enters on turn 3 as a 2/2 enchantment creature (its mana value), and its "Creatures lose
# all abilities" takes its own abilities as well as every other creature's, while its effect goes on applying (CR 613.6):
# its enters trigger is not there to trigger (CR 603.6a), so Bot1 draws nothing, and it is not sacrificed at the end step -
# on turn 5 it is still on the battlefield. Bot1's Llanowar Elves taps for {G} before it (turn 3, the positive control) and
# has no mana ability under it: the refusal on turn 5, untapped and long past summoning sickness, holds.

